<title>COTE D'IVOIRE: Blast closes Nescafe Ivorian plant, one killed.</title>
<headline>Blast closes Nescafe Ivorian plant, one killed.</headline>
<dateline>ABIDJAN 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>A boiler explosion halted production at a Nestle soluble coffee plant in Ivory Coast at the weekend, a factory spokeswoman said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;Production has stopped, but we expect to open next week,&quot; finance director Virginie Medase told Reuters. &quot;One man was killed.&quot;</p>
<p>The cause of the blast on Sunday afternoon was being investigated.</p>
<p>Nescafe Cote d'Ivoire processed around 24,000 tonnes of green robusta beans and manufactured around 9,500 tonnes of soluble coffee in 1996/97, Medase said.</p>
<p>A coffee roasting plant on the same site had not been affected, she added.</p>
<p>-- Matthew Bunce, Abidjan newsroom + 225 21 90 90</p>
